\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The documentary record for the compounds this paper treats as simulants. Standing is graded by what the document does: \emph  {designated} names the compound for a stated measurement, \emph  {recorded} notes that it has been used without naming a measurement to validate it against, and \emph  {none} means no instrument was found. The measurement each compound is used for now is detection by a sensor, except in the last block, which lists two compounds the same NIOSH document names for filtration and which neither panel carries; they are shown because the rule by which the primary panel was built would have admitted them.}}{16}{}\protected@file@percent }
